{"id":244052552147428,"type":"album","name":"A Ghost Is Born","artist":"Wilco","year":2004,"weight":17,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/346-a-ghost-is-born_190526.jpg","aoty":77,"aoty_user":80,"yt":"cpAw672ys7Y","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/wilco/a-ghost-is-born","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/346-wilco-a-ghost-is-born.php"},"desc":"A Ghost Is Born is the fifth studio album by Chicago-based alternative rock band Wilco. Released on June 22, 2004, it features singer Jeff Tweedy on lead guitar more than any previous Wilco album. The band streamed the album online for free, and offered a five song EP to purchasers. Tweedy entered a rehab clinic shortly before the release of the album, delaying its release by two weeks. It also shortened its promotional tour. Despite this, A Ghost Is Born's opening week was the best sales week for the band at the time and the album was met with good ."},"artist_ref":{"id":60918958327409,"name":"Wilco","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wilco_MassMoca_AustinNelson.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":150286518426001,"type":"genre","name":"Chicago School","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":25982342537682,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Chicago School","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":5,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":208356503087556,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Art Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":107,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":89365250498738,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Indie Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":199,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":44735175437010,"name":"AOTY Must Hear 2000s","src":"charts","grp":"AOTY","list_year":null,"rank":305,"year":2004,"note":null,"total":520,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album was recorded during a period when Jeff Tweedy was severely struggling with crippling migraines, panic attacks, and a painkiller addiction, leading him to believe he was going to die. The album includes a track that audibly represents the onset of a migraine. \"When Wilco was recording their 2003 album, A Ghost is Born, things were really, really bad. Vicodin attacks, migraines, benches on painkillers and at one point Jeff was convinced he was going to die.\"","year":2003,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Musicians Battling Disease Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uzIMWVbi-GM"}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":48256840353553,"type":"album","name":"Being There","year":1996,"weight":34},{"id":56347474376684,"type":"album","name":"Yankee Hotel Foxtrot","year":2002,"weight":30},{"id":85254963667669,"type":"album","name":"Summerteeth","year":1999,"weight":22},{"id":153536828298661,"type":"album","name":"Sky Blue Sky","year":2007,"weight":10},{"id":183878052086014,"type":"song","name":"Either Way","year":2007,"weight":7},{"id":173241179310473,"type":"song","name":"Less Than You Think","year":2003,"weight":7},{"id":23262094967375,"type":"song","name":"Record Labels","year":2011,"weight":7},{"id":170532541714832,"type":"album","name":"Summer Teeth","year":1999,"weight":6},{"id":276234429296869,"type":"album","name":"AM (Re-edition)","year":null,"weight":4},{"id":271298912172317,"type":"album","name":"Cruel Country","year":2022,"weight":4},{"id":149118570349218,"type":"album","name":"A.M.","year":1995,"weight":4},{"id":68883418041703,"type":"album","name":"Being There (Re-edition)","year":null,"weight":4}]}